    {
      "id": "gold-02-pleasure",
      "stepLabel": "01 GOLD — Part 1",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "God’s pleasure and purpose",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Just as artists express themselves through their talents, God takes pleasure in His creation. The Bible reveals that God created everything for Himself, choosing humanity to express His love. Although God is perfect and reveals Himself through His creation, He cannot dwell with sin, and no sin is allowed in heaven."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Everything belongs to Him, but He created us not out of narcissism, but for an intimate relationship that blesses us beyond our imagination."
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
        {
          "type": "next",
          "label": "Continue",
          "nodeId": "gold-02-pleasure-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gold-03-holiness",
      "stepLabel": "01 GOLD — Part 2",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "Holiness and obedience",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Although He created mankind in His image and loves us more than anything else He made, He demands our obedience."
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
        {
          "type": "next",
          "label": "Continue",
          "nodeId": "gold-03-holiness-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gold-scripture-1jn416",
      "stepLabel": "01 GOLD — Scripture",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "1 John 4:16",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And we have known and believed the love that God has for us. God is love, and he who abides in love abides in God, and God in him. [1 John 4:16]"
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
