    {
      "id": "red-02-cross",
      "stepLabel": "03 RED — Part 1",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "God’s plan in Christ",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Before creation, God had a plan to save us. To fulfill His justice, He sent His Son, Jesus, to become a man and live a sinless life. Rather than convicting Him of sin as it does for us, the law revealed His righteousness, declaring Him a perfect man and God's perfect sacrifice for sin. He didn't die for His sins; instead, He took on ours and suffered the punishment we deserved, becoming a sacrifice for the world's sins."
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
        {
          "type": "next",
          "label": "Continue",
          "nodeId": "red-02-cross-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "red-03-finished",
      "stepLabel": "03 RED — Part 2",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "Finished",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Jesus endured the wrath of God, died, and was forsaken by the Father. God raised Him from the dead, and now, through faith, we can be forgiven because Jesus paid our debts. Before His last breath on the cross, Jesus declared, 'It is finished,' signifying that God reconciled the world to Himself through His Son."
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
        {
          "type": "next",
          "label": "Continue",
          "nodeId": "red-03-finished-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "red-scripture-1cor1534",
      "stepLabel": "03 RED — Scripture",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "1 Corinthians 15:3–4",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Gospel (Good News)...that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures, and that He was buried, and that He rose again the third day according to the Scriptures. [1 Corinthians 15:3-4]"
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
        {
