    {
      "id": "light-02-righteousness",
      "stepLabel": "04 LIGHT — Teaching",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "Only Jesus is good enough",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "We often deceive ourselves into thinking we are 'good enough' for heaven, but that isn't true. Only Jesus is good enough to reach heaven. He taught that our righteousness must exceed that of the religious leaders, who also fell short. Unlike other religions, Christians depend on Jesus for salvation. God promises that if we believe in His Son and accept salvation through Jesus' sacrifice and resurrection, we will be regarded as His children, with His righteousness credited to us by faith. Though we don't deserve heaven, we can enter because Jesus forgives and cleanses us from our unrighteousness when we trust in Him. Salvation is a free gift that cannot be earned."
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
      "buttons": [
        {
          "type": "next",
          "label": "Continue",
          "nodeId": "light-02-righteousness-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "light-scripture-acts412",
      "stepLabel": "04 LIGHT — Scripture",
      "layout": "stamped",
      "title": "Acts 4:12",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Nor is there salvation in any other, for there is no other name under heaven given among men by which we must be saved. [Acts 4:12]"
        }
      ],
      "media": [],
